ell types from the same blood sample  similar to our untouched pbmc isolation  products  the protocol for straight from is very  similar independent of the specific  starting materials that you work with  no matter if we're talking about whole  blood  buffy coats lrscs or glucopacks first  you fill the blood sample into a  collection tube  next straight from microbeads are added  and then you incubate for 15 minutes in  the fridge  then the magnetic separation is done on  the multi-max separator or in the case  of whole blood you can also use the auto  max pro separator  in both cases it takes just 30 minutes  from the blood sample to you holding  your target cells in the hand  straights foam is based on a positive  isolation approach from the starting  material and this provides a very  attractive advantage  this advantage would be how positive  selection enables consecutive  separations from the same sample  by using the negative fraction for  another round of separation  here we have an example first you  isolate  cd8 positive t cells and then take the  negative fraction  for isolation of cd4 positive cells  you could take this even another step  further and isolate another round of  subpopulations from that negative  fraction  therefore if you're interested in  several target cell populations from the  same blood sample  this may be the ideal product for your  experiment  a frequent question that we encounter  when discussing our positive selection  reagents has to do with the  performance and downstream functionality  of the cells that are isolated  in this case we've checked for t cell  enrichment  t-cell activation and transduction  efficiency as compared to  density gradient centrifugation and as  expected  we have comparable results but of course  the t cells and the separation were done  much faster using the straight from  approach  this means that our isolation will allow  you to choose the cells of interest  with no negative side effects on your  downstream results  but allowing you to be more efficient at  the same time  in this next section i will talk about  automating your cell isolation  workflow now why do we actually  need automation what is the advantage  as we've already said a little earlier  automation reduces hands-on time and  frees you up to work on other tasks in  the meantime that can't be automated  it minimizes the variation between  different users in the lab or  even a good or bad day from the same  individual  and of course it minimizes costly human  errors  with standard protocols and minimum user  variation  you can be sure that the effects that  you're seeing are due to your assay  rather than artifacts  in short automation reduces redundant  experiments and allows you to focus your  time where it matters  when introducing our family of automated  cell separators we'll start with the  auto max pro  the easy to use bench top instrument for  every laboratory  with fully automated sequential  separation of one to six samples  the auto max provides easy access to the  automation without  high investment costs or lots of  training you can mix  many different starting materials and  samples within one run  and just hit the button and the  instrument will label and separate the  cells for you  the columns are reusable so maintenance  is easy  and column cost can be reduced the  instrument is the perfect match for the  isolation of pbmcs from peripheral blood  and buffy coats  but of course also target cells that can  be isolated from pvmcs within the auto  max pro  if you are interested in isolating  multiple samples in parallel  the multi-max family is a perfect fit  for this  24 magnets allow you to process between  1 and 24 samples in a single run  or split or split your large samples  between multiple columns  this is achieved by using the ls ld or  whole blood columns  or the multi 24 column block for easy  easy handling of 24 samples or perhaps a  very large sample  like an entire leukopak the multi-max  cell 24 is a  semi-automated instrument that is a good  fit for many labs that  value easy handling but don't mind the  manual pipetting  however if you want full automation and  maximum throughput  you will love the multi-max x which  integrates the multi-max into a liquid  handler  the multi-max x is the instrument for  the high demanding  high-throughput cell processing lab  samples are labeled and isolated  automatically  both for pbmc generation or  subpopulations from all blood products  all programs are tailored to match your  needs so you can be confident  that you will be satisfied with the  protocol and the results delivered from  this instrument  so we're coming to the end of the  presentation and there are a few things  that i want you to keep in mind when  thinking about  density gradient free solutions for cell  isolation with max technology  it should be no secret that the success  of any experiment depends on the quality  of the starting material  so remember that the right cell  preparation and isolation steps are  crucial  in the beginning of any workflow to  ensure reliable assay results  automating these processes with the help  of our cell separation instruments  combined with our density gradient free  protocols  allow you to be more efficient while  ensuring high reproducibility and  standardization  our new methods enable you to isolate  target cells or pbmcs directly from  blood products with high speed  great performance and easy protocols  i'd like to thank everyone for attending  this webinar  and for the latest updates and resources  available for drug discovery workflows  please come by the booth or stop by our  website  thank you and take care
 

